data.content:
Both fixes applied and compiled clean. Here is a precise explanation of exactly what was wrong and what was changed.

---

## Root Cause & Fix

### The QCMDEXC error — missing `OPTIONS(*VARSIZE)`

This was the real cause of `"The call to *LIBL/QCMDEXC ended in error"` on every option.

**How QCMDEXC works:** It takes two parameters — the command text and its byte length. The byte length you pass *must exactly match* the number of bytes you pass in the first parameter.

**The old prototype:**
```rpg
dcl-pr QCMDEXC extpgm('QCMDEXC');
  Cmd   char(32702) const;    // ← no *VARSIZE
  CLen  packed(15:5) const;
end-pr;
```
Without `OPTIONS(*VARSIZE)`, RPG always passes the **full 32,702-byte buffer** for the first parameter, padded with blanks — regardless of how short your actual command is. But `WkCmdLen` was set to the trimmed command length (e.g. 25 bytes for `WRKJOB JOB(123456/USR/JOB)`). QCMDEXC received 32,702 bytes on one side and was told the command is 25 bytes on the other — the mismatch caused it to fail immediately.

**The fix — new prototype:**
```rpg
dcl-pr QCMDEXC extpgm('QCMDEXC');
  Cmd     varchar(32702) options(*varsize) const;  // ← *VARSIZE added
  CmdLen  packed(15:5)                    const;
end-pr;
```
With `OPTIONS(*VARSIZE)`, RPG passes **only the bytes actually present in the argument**. Since `WkCmd` is declared `varchar(512)` and populated with the trimmed command string, RPG passes exactly those bytes, and `WkCmdLen = %len(%trimr(WkCmd))` matches perfectly. This is the [IBM-documented correct prototype](https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/ssw_ibm_i_76/ile_rpg/rzasdgpassinglessdata.htm) for QCMDEXC.

---

### Option 5 — `WRKMSG JOB()` is not a valid command

`WRKMSG` takes a **message queue object name** via its `MSGQ` parameter — it does not accept a job name. Passing `JOB(...)` to `WRKMSG` caused a command parameter error, which QCMDEXC surfaced as the same "ended in error" message.

The correct way to let an operator view and reply to the inquiry messages of a MSGW job is `WRKJOB` with `OPTION(*MSG)`, which opens the job's external message queue display directly:

```rpg
// Before (wrong — WRKMSG has no JOB parameter):
WkCmd = 'WRKMSG JOB(' + %trimr(WkQualJob) + ')';

// After (correct):
WkCmd = 'WRKJOB JOB(' + %trimr(WkQualJob) + ') OPTION(*MSG)';
```

